{
  "title": "Ziyarat of Imam Ali (a.s.) on the Prophet's (s.a.w.a.) Birthday — Najaf",
  "data": "Before the visit, perform ghusl, put on your cleanest clothes, wear perfume and walk to the shrine calmly and with dignity.\nAt Bab al-Salam, the gate of the shrine, face the qibla and say 3 times:\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nALLAAHU AKBAR\nAllah is the Most Great.\nThen, still at the gate, say:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon the Messenger of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى خِيَرَةِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA KHIYARATILLAAH\nPeace be upon the elite select of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْبَشِيْرِ النَّذِيْرِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL BASHEERIN NADHEER\nPeace be upon the bearer of glad tidings, the warner (against Allah’s chastisement),\nالسِّرَاجِ الْمُنِيْرِ\nAS-SIRAAJIL MUNEER\nand the shining lantern.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAllah’s mercy and blessings be upon him.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الطُّهْرِ الطَّاهِرِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAT TUHRIT TAAHIR\nPeace be upon the pure, the immaculate.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْعَلَمِ الزَّاهِرِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL A'LAMIZ ZAAHIR\nPeace be upon the luminous epitome.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمَنْصُوْرِ الْمُؤَيَّدِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL MANSOORIL MU'AYYAD\nPeace be upon the one given victory and aid (by Almighty Allah).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَبِي الْقَاسِمِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA ABIL QAASIMI MUHAMMAD\nPeace be upon Abu’l-Qasim Muhammad.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAllah’s mercy and blessings be upon him.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَنْبِيَاۤءِ اللّٰهِ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA ANBIYAA'ILLAAHIL MURSALEEN\nPeace be upon the missioned Prophets of Allah\nوَعِبَادِ اللّٰهِ الصَّالِحِيْنَ\nWA I'BAADILLAAHIS SAALIHEEN\nand upon the righteous servants of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَلَاۤئِكَةِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA MALAA'IKATILLAAH\nPeace be upon the angels of Allah\nالْحَآفِّيْنَ بِهٰذَا الْحَرَمِ\nAL-HAAFFEENA BIHAADHAL HARAM\nwho surround this sanctuary\nوَبِهٰذَا الضَّرِيْحِ اللَّاۤئِذِيْنَ بِهٖ\nWA BIHAADHAD DAREEHIL LAA'IDHEENA BIH\nand this tomb to which they are resorting.\nApproach the tomb and say:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَصِيَّ الْاَوْصِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WASIYYAL AWSIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O successor of the Prophets’ successors.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عِمَادَ الْاَتْقِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA I'MAADAL ATQIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O reliance of the pious ones.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَلِيَّ الْاَوْلِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WALIYYAL AWLIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O best saint among all saints.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا سَيِّدَ الشُّهَدَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAYYIDASH SHUHADAA'\nPeace be upon you, O master of martyrs.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اٰيَةَ اللّٰهِ الْعُظْمٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA AAYATALLAAHIL U'ZMAA\nPeace be upon you, O grandest sign of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَامِسَ اَهْلِ الْعَبَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA KHAAMISA AHLIL A'BAA'\nPeace be upon you, O fifth of the People of the Cloak.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا قَاۤئِدَ الْغُرِّ الْمُحَجَّلِيْنَ الْاَتْقِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA QAA'IDAL GHURRIL MUHAJJALEENAL ATQIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O leader of the white-forehead, pious group.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عِصْمَةَ الْاَوْلِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA I'SMATAL AWLIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O shelter of the saints.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا زَيْنَ الْمُوَحِّدِيْنَ النُّجَبَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA ZAYNAL MUWAHHIDEENAN NUJABAA'\nPeace be upon you, O adornment of the noble monotheists.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَالِصَ الْاَخِلَّاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA KHAALISAL AKHILLAA'\nPeace be upon you, O select of the best friends.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَالِدَ الْاَئِمَّةِ الْاُمَنَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAALIDAL A'IMMATIL UMANAA'\nPeace be upon you, O father of the trusted Imams.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَاحِبَ الْحَوْضِ وَحَامِلَ اللِّوَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAAHIBAL HAWDI WA HAAMILAL LIWAA'\nPeace be upon you, O director of the (Divine) pond and bearer of the Pennon.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا قَسِيْمَ الْجَنَّةِ وَلَظٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA QASEEMAL JANNATI WA LAZAA\nPeace be upon you, O decider of Paradise and Hellfire—the flaming.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ شُرِّفَتْ بِهٖ مَكَّةُ وَمِنٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN SHURRIFAT BIHEE MAKKATU WA MINAA\nPeace be upon you, O one by whom Makkah and Mina have been honored.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بَحْرَ الْعُلُوْمِ وَكَنَفَ الْفُقَرَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA BAHRAL U'LOOMI WA KANAFAL FUQARAA'\nPeace be upon you, O ocean of knowledge and haven of the poor.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ وُلِدَ فِي الْكَعْبَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN WULIDA FIL KA'BAH\nPeace be upon you, O one who was born in the Ka'bah,\nوَزُوِّجَ فِي السَّمَاۤءِ بِسَيِّدَةِ النِّسَاۤءِ\nWA ZUWWIJA FIS SAMAA'I BISAYYIDATIN NISAA'\nmarried in the heavens to the Doyenne of Women;\nوَكَانَ شُهُوْدُهَا الْمَلَاۤئِكَةَ الْاَصْفِيَاۤءَ\nWA KAANA SHUHOODUHAL MALAA'IKATAL ASFIYAA'\nand the witnesses were the elite angels.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مِصْبَاحَ الضِّيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MISBAAHAD DIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O lantern of light.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ خَصَّهُ النَّبِيُّ بِجَزِيْلِ الْحِبَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN KHASSAHUN NABIYYU BIJAZEELIL HIBAA'\nPeace be upon you, O he whom the Prophet singled out for abundant gifts.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ بَاتَ عَلٰى فِرَاشِ خَاتَمِ الْاَنْبِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN BAATA A'LAA FIRAASHI KHAATAMIL ANBIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O one who replaced the Seal of the Prophets in his bed\nوَوَقَاهُ بِنَفْسِهٖ شَرَّ الْاَعْدَاۤءِ\nWA WAQAAHU BINAFSIHEE SHARRAL A'DAA'\nand protected him with his soul against the evil of the enemies.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ رُدَّتْ لَهُ الشَّمْسُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN RUDDAT LAHUSH SHAMS\nPeace be upon you, O one to whom the sun was returned\nفَسَامٰى شَمْعُوْنَ الصَّفَا\nFASAAMAA SHAM'OONAS SAFAA\nand he thus became the match of Sham'un al-Safa (Simon Peter).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ اَنْجَى اللّٰهُ سَفِيْنَةَ نُوْحٍ بِاسْمِهٖ وَاسْمِ اَخِيْهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN ANJALLAAHU SAFEENATA NOOHIN BISMIHEE WASMI AKHEEH\nPeace be upon you, O one in whose name and in the name of whose brother, Allah saved the Ark of Noah\nحَيْثُ الْتَطَمَ الْمَاۤءُ حَوْلَهَا وَطَمٰى\nHAYTHUL TATAMAL MAA'U HAWLAHAA WA TAMAA\nwhen the waves of water collided and clashed around it.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ تَابَ اللّٰهُ بِهٖ وَبِاَخِيْهِ عَلٰى اٰدَمَ اِذْ غَوٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN TAABALLAAHU BIHEE WA BI-AKHEEHI A'LAA AADAMA IDH GHAWAA\nPeace be upon you, O one in whose name and in the name of whose brother, Allah accepted the repentance of Adam after he had allowed himself to be seduced.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا فُلْكَ النَّجَاةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA FULKAN NAJAAH\nPeace be upon you, O ark of redemption;\nالَّذِيْ مَنْ رَكِبَهٗ نَجَا\nALLADHEE MAN RAKIBAHOO NAJAA\nhe who embarks on it will have saved himself (from perdition),\nوَمَنْ تَاَخَّرَ عَنْهُ هَوٰى\nWA MAN TA'AKHKHARA A'NHU HAWAA\nbut he who leaves it will have perished.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ خَاطَبَ الثُّعْبَانَ وَذِئْبَ الْفَلَا\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN KHAATABATH THU'BAANA WA DHI'BAL FALAA\nPeace be upon you, O he who spoke to a serpent and to a wolf in the desert.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اَمِيْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA AMEERAL MU'MINEEN\nPeace be upon you, O commander of the faithful.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAllah’s mercy and blessings be upon you.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حُجَّةَ اللّٰهِ عَلٰى مَنْ كَفَرَ وَاَنَابَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HUJJATALLAAHI A'LAA MAN KAFARA WA ANAAB\nPeace be upon you, O argument of Allah against those who disbelieved and those who turned (to Him).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اِمَامَ ذَوِي الْاَلْبَابِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA IMAAMA DHAWIL ALBAAB\nPeace be upon you, O chief of people of understanding.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَعْدِنَ الْحِكْمَةِ وَفَصْلَ الْخِطَابِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MA'DINAL HIKMATI WA FASLAL KHITAAB\nPeace be upon you, O essence of wisdom and clear judgment.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ عِنْدَهٗ عِلْمُ الْكِتَابِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN I'NDAHOO I'LMUL KITAAB\nPeace be upon you, O one having the knowledge of the Books.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مِيْزَانَ يَوْمِ الْحِسَابِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MEEZAANA YAWMIL HISAAB\nPeace be upon you, O criterion on the Judgment Day.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا فَاصِلَ الْحُكْمِ النَّاطِقَ بِالصَّوَابِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA FAASILAL HUKMIN NAATIQA BIS SAWAAB\nPeace be upon you, O solver of all quarrels and spokesman of truth.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْمُتَصَدِّقُ بِالْخَاتَمِ فِي الْمِحْرَابِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL MUTASADDIQU BIL KHAATAMI FIL MIHRAAB\nPeace be upon you, O he who gave his ring as alms while being in the prayer niche.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ كَفَى اللّٰهُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN KAFALLAAHUL MU'MINEEN\nPeace be upon you, O he through whom Allah sufficed the believers\nالْقِتَالَ بِهٖ يَوْمَ الْاَحْزَابِ\nAL-QITAALA BIHEE YAWMAL AHZAAB\nin fighting on the Battle of al-Ahzab (the Allies).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ اَخْلَصَ لِلّٰهِ الْوَحْدَانِيَّةَ وَاَنَابَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN AKHLASA LILLAAHIL WAHDAANIYYATA WA ANAAB\nPeace be upon you, O he who worshipped Allah alone with sincerity and always turned to Him.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا قَاتِلَ خَيْبَرَ وَقَالِعَ الْبَابِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA QAATILA KHAYBARA WA QAALI'AL BAAB\nPeace be upon you, O warrior of Khaybar and plucker of the gate (of the fortress).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ دَعَاهُ خَيْرُ الْاَنَامِ لِلْمَبِيْتِ عَلٰى فِرَاشِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN DA'AAHU KHAYRUL ANAAMI LIL MABEETI A'LAA FIRAASHIH\nPeace be upon you, O one who, when the Best of Creatures (i.e. the Prophet) ordered him to spend that night at his place instead of him,\nفَاَسْلَمَ نَفْسَهٗ لِلْمَنِيَّةِ وَاَجَابَ\nFA-ASLAMA NAFSAHOO LIL MANIYYATI WA AJAAB\nsubmitted to death and responded.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ لَهٗ طُوْبٰى وَحُسْنُ مَاٰبٍ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN LAHOO TOOBAA WA HUSNU MA'AAB\nPeace be upon you, O he for whom are Tuba (bliss) and a goodly return.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAllah’s mercy and blessings be upon you.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَلِيَّ عِصْمَةِ الدِّيْنِ وَيَا سَيِّدَ السَّادَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WALIYYA I'SMATID DEENI WA YAA SAYYIDAS SAADAAT\nPeace be upon you, O director of the safety of the religion and chief of the chiefs.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَاحِبَ الْمُعْجِزَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAAHIBAL MU'JIZAAT\nPeace be upon you, O owner of miracles.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ نَزَلَتْ فِي فَضْلِهٖ سُوْرَةُ الْعَادِيَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN NAZALAT FEE FADLIHEE SOORATUL A'ADIYAAT\nPeace be upon you, O he about whose merits Surah al-'Adiyat was revealed.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ كُتِبَ اسْمُهٗ فِي السَّمَاۤءِ عَلَى السُّرَادِقَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN KUTIBAS MUHOO FIS SAMAA'I A'LAS SURAADIQAAT\nPeace be upon you, O he whose name is written in the heavens on the canopies (of the Divine Throne).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُظْهِرَ الْعَجَاۤئِبِ وَالْاٰيَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MUZHIRAL A'JAA'IBI WAL AAYAAT\nPeace be upon you, O manifester of marvels and signs.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اَمِيْرَ الْغَزَوَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA AMEERAL GHAZAWAAT\nPeace be upon you, O commander in campaigns.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُخْبِرًا بِمَا غَبَرَ وَبِمَا هُوَ اٰتٍ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MUKHBIRAN BIMAA GHABARA WA BIMAA HUWA AAT\nPeace be upon you, O he who accounted the bygone and predicted the future.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُخَاطِبَ ذِئْبِ الْفَلَوَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MUKHAATIBA DHI'BIL FALAWAAT\nPeace be upon you, O speaker to a wolf in the desert.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَاتِمَ الْحَصٰى وَمُبَيِّنَ الْمُشْكِلَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA KHAATIMAL HASAA WA MUBAYYINAL MUSHKILAAT\nPeace be upon you, O sealer of the pebbles and expounder of problems.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ عَجِبَتْ مِنْ حَمَلَاتِهٖ فِي الْوَغٰى مَلَاۤئِكَةُ السَّمَاوَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN A'JIBAT MIN HAMALAATIHEE FIL WAGHAA MALAA'IKATUS SAMAAWAAT\nPeace be upon you, O he whose attacks in battlefields astonished the angels in the heavens.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ نَاجَى الرَّسُوْلَ فَقَدَّمَ بَيْنَ يَدَيْ نَجْوَاهُ الصَّدَقَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN NAAJAR RASOOLA FAQADDAMA BAYNA YADAY NAJWAAHUS SADAQAAT\nPeace be upon you, O he who offered something in charity when he talked confidentially with the Messenger.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَالِدَ الْاَئِمَّةِ الْبَرَرَةِ السَّادَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAALIDAL A'IMMATIL BARARATIS SAADAAT\nPeace be upon you, O father of the Imams, the virtuous masters.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAllah’s mercy and blessings be upon you.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا تَالِيَ الْمَبْعُوْثِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA TAALIYAL MAB'OOTH\nPeace be upon you, O one coming immediately after the Messenger.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ عِلْمِ خَيْرِ مَوْرُوْثٍ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA I'LMI KHAYRI MAWROOTH\nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of the knowledge of the most favorable inherited being.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAllah’s mercy and blessings be upon you.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا سَيِّدَ الْوَصِيِّيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAYYIDAL WASIYYEEN\nPeace be upon you, O chief of the Prophets’ successors.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اِمَامَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA IMAAMAL MUTTAQEEN\nPeace be upon you, O head of the pious ones.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا غِيَاثَ الْمَكْرُوْبِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA GHIYAATHAL MAKROOBEEN\nPeace be upon you, O aid of the aggrieved ones.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عِصْمَةَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA I'SMATAL MU'MINEEN\nPeace be upon you, O shelter of the believers.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُظْهِرَ الْبَرَاهِيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MUZHIRAL BARAAHEEN\nPeace be upon you, O provider of evidences.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا طٰهٰ وَيٰسٓ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA TAA HAA WA YAA SEEN\nPeace be upon you, O Ta-Ha and Ya-Sin.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حَبْلَ اللّٰهِ الْمَتِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HABLALLAAHIL MATEEN\nPeace be upon you, O firm rope (taking) to Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ تَصَدَّقَ فِي صَلَاتِهٖ بِخَاتَمِهٖ عَلَى الْمِسْكِيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN TASADDAQA FEE SALAATIHEE BIKHAATAMIHEE A'LAL MISKEEN\nPeace be upon you, O he who gave his ring as alms, while he was offering prayer, to a poor.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا قَالِعَ الصَّخْرَةِ عَنْ فَمِ الْقَلِيبِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA QAALI'AS SAKHRATI A'N FAMIL QALEEB\nPeace be upon you, O he who removed the rock from the open of the well,\nوَمُظْهِرَ الْمَاۤءِ الْمَعِيْنِ\nWA MUZHIRAL MAA'IL MA'EEN\nand he thus caused the pure water to flow.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَيْنَ اللّٰهِ النَّاظِرَةَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'YNALLAAHIN NAAZIRAH\nPeace be upon you, O observing eye of Allah,\nوَيَدَهُ الْبَاسِطَةَ\nWA YADAHUL BAASITAH\nHis extended Hand,\nوَلِسَانَهُ الْمُعَبِّرَ عَنْهُ فِيْ بَرِيَّتِهٖ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nWA LISAANAHUL MU'ABBIRA A'NHU FEE BARIYYATIHEE AJMA'EEN\nand His spokesman who conveys His affairs to all of His created beings.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ عِلْمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA I'LMIN NABIYYEEN\nPeace be upon you, O heir of the Prophets’ knowledge,\nوَمُسْتَوْدَعَ عِلْمِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْاٰخِرِيْنَ\nWA MUSTAWDA'A I'LMIL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREEN\nkeeper of the knowledge of the past and coming generations,\nوَصَاحِبَ لِوَاۤءِ الْحَمْدِ\nWA SAAHIBA LIWAA'IL HAMD\nbearer of the Pennon of Praise (liwa’ al-hamd),\nوَسَاقِيَ اَوْلِيَاۤئِهٖ مِنْ حَوْضِ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nWA SAAQIYA AWLIYAA'IHEE MIN HAWDI KHAATAMIN NABIYYEEN\nand one who shall serve his adherents with water from the (Divine) Pond of the Seal of the Prophets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا يَعْسُوْبَ الدِّيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA YA'SOOBAD DEEN\nPeace be upon you, O head of the religion,\nوَقَاۤئِدَ الْغُرِّ الْمُحَجَّلِيْنَ\nWA QAA'IDAL GHURRIL MUHAJJALEEN\nleader of the white-forehead group,\nوَوَالِدَ الْاَئِمَّةِ الْمَرْضِيِّيْنَ\nWA WAALIDAL A'IMMATIL MARDIYYEEN\nand father of the well-pleased Imams.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAllah’s mercy and blessings be upon you.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى اسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّضِيِّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAS MILLAAHIR RADIYY\nPeace be upon the pleased name of Allah,\nوَوَجْهِهِ الْمُضِيۤءِ\nWA WAJHIHIL MUDEE'\nHis radiant Face,\nوَجَنْبِهِ الْقَوِيِّ\nWA JANBIHIL QAWIYY\nHis strong Side,\nوَصِرَاطِهِ السَّوِيِّ\nWA SIRAATIHIS SAWIYY\nand His straight Path.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْاِمَامِ التَّقِيِّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL IMAAMIT TAQIYY\nPeace be upon the pious Imam,\nالْمُخْلِصِ الصَّفِيِّ\nAL-MUKHLISIS SAFIYY\nthe sincere, the elite.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْكَوْكَبِ الدُّرِّيِّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL KAWKABID DURRIYY\nPeace be upon the brightly shining star.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْاِمَامِ اَبِي الْحَسَنِ عَلِيٍّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL IMAAMI ABIL HASANI A'LIYY\nPeace be upon the Imam Abu’l-Hasan 'Ali.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAllah’s mercy and blessings be upon him.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَئِمَّةِ الْهُدٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA A'IMMATIL HUDAA\nPeace be upon the leaders to true guidance,\nوَمَصَابِيْحِ الدُّجٰى\nWA MASAABEEHID DUJAA\nthe lanterns in murk,\nوَاَعْلَامِ التُّقٰى\nWA A'LAAMIT TUQAA\nthe epitomes of piety,\nوَمَنَارِ الْهُدٰى\nWA MANAARIL HUDAA\nthe lights of true guidance,\nوَذَوِي النُّهٰى\nWA DHAWIN NUHAA\nand owners of thought,\nوَكَهْفِ الْوَرٰى\nWA KAHFIL WARAA\nthe havens of people,\nوَالْعُرْوَةِ الْوُثْقٰى\nWAL U'RWATIL WUTHQAA\nthe firmest handles,\nوَالْحُجَّةِ عَلٰىۤ اَهْلِ الدُّنْيَا\nWAL HUJJATI A'LAA AHLID DUNYAA\nand the arguments against the inhabitants of this world.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAllah’s mercy and blessings be upon them.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى نُوْرِ الْاَنْوَارِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA NOORIL ANWAAR\nPeace be upon the light of lights,\nوَحُجَّةِ الْجَبَّارِ\nWA HUJJATIL JABBAAR\nthe argument of the Omnipotent Lord,\nوَوَالِدِ الْاَئِمَّةِ الْاَطْهَارِ\nWA WAALIDIL A'IMMATIL AT-HAAR\nthe father of the immaculate Imams,\nوَقَسِيْمِ الْجَنَّةِ وَالنَّارِ\nWA QASEEMIL JANNATI WAN NAAR\nthe decider of Paradise and Hellfire,\nالْمُخْبِرِ عَنِ الْاٰثَارِ\nAL-MUKHBIRI A'NIL AATHAAR\nthe narrator of past events,\nالْمُدَمِّرِ عَلَى الْكُفَّارِ\nAL-MUDAMMIRI A'LAL KUFFAAR\nthe destroyer of the unbelievers,\nمُسْتَنْقِذِ الشِّيْعَةِ الْمُخْلِصِيْنَ مِنْ عَظِيْمِ الْاَوْزَارِ\nMUSTANQIDHISH SHEE'ATIL MUKHLISEENA MIN A'ZEEMIL AWZAAR\nand the savior of the faithful Shi'ah from their grand sins.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمَخْصُوْصِ بِالطَّاهِرَةِ التَّقِيَّةِ ابْنَةِ الْمُخْتَارِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL MAKHSOOSI BIT TAAHIRATIT TAQIYYATIBNATIL MUKHTAAR\nPeace be upon the one singled out for the pure, pious daughter of the Chosen Prophet,\nالْمَوْلُوْدِ فِي الْبَيْتِ ذِي الْاَسْتَارِ\nAL-MAWLOODI FIL BAYTI DHIL ASTAAR\nthe one born in the House of curtains,\nالْمُزَوَّجِ فِي السَّمَاۤءِ بِالْبَرَّةِ الطَّاهِرَةِ\nAL-MUZAWWAJI FIS SAMAA'I BIL BARRATIT TAAHIRAH\nthe one married in the heavens to the reverent, immaculate,\nالرَّضِيَّةِ الْمَرْضِيَّةِ\nAR-RADIYYATIL MARDIYYAH\ncontent, and well-pleased lady—\nوَالِدَةِ الْاَئِمَّةِ الْاَطْهَارِ\nWAALIDATIL A'IMMATIL AT-HAAR\nthe mother of the immaculate Imams.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAllah’s mercy and blessings be upon him.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى النَّبَاِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAN NABA'IL A'ZEEM\nPeace be upon the Great News,\nالَّذِيْ هُمْ فِيْهِ مُخْتَلِفُوْنَ\nALLADHEE HUM FEEHI MUKHTALIFOON\nabout whom they differ,\nوَعَلَيْهِ يُعْرَضُوْنَ\nWA A'LAYHI YU'RADOON\nbefore whom they shall be presented,\nوَعَنْهُ يُسْاَلُوْنَ\nWA A'NHU YUS'ALOON\nand about whom they shall be asked.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى نُوْرِ اللّٰهِ الْاَنْوَرِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA NOORILLAAHIL ANWAR\nPeace be upon the most shining light of Allah\nوَضِيَاۤئِهِ الْاَزْهَرِ\nWA DIYAA'IHIL AZHAR\nand the most luminous brightness of Him.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAllah’s mercy and blessings be upon him.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَلِيَّ اللّٰهِ وَحُجَّتَهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WALIYYALLAAHI WA HUJJATAH\nPeace be upon you, O Allah’s friend and argument\nوَخَالِصَةَ اللّٰهِ وَخَآصَّتَهٗ\nWA KHAALISATALLAAHI WA KHAASSATAH\nand Allah’s select and choice.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ يَا وَلِيَّ اللّٰهِ وَحُجَّتَهٗ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA YAA WALIYYALLAAHI WA HUJJATAH\nI bear witness that you, being Allah’s friend and argument,\nلَقَدْ جَاهَدْتَ فِي سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ حَقَّ جِهَادِهٖ\nLAQAD JAAHADTA FEE SABEELILLAAHI HAQQA JIHAADIH\nstrove in Allah’s way in the most appropriate way,\nوَاتَّبَعْتَ مِنْهَاجَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nWATTABA'TA MINHAAJA RASOOLILLAAHI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nfollowed the course of Allah’s Messenger, peace be upon him and his Household,\nوَحَلَّلْتَ حَلَالَ اللّٰهِ\nWA HALLALTA HALAALALLAAH\ndeemed lawful that which Allah has made lawful,\nوَحَرَّمْتَ حَرَامَ اللّٰهِ\nWA HARRAMTA HARAAMALLAAH\ndeemed unlawful that which Allah has made unlawful,\nوَشَرَعْتَ اَحْكَامَهٗ\nWA SHARA'TA AHKAAMAH\ncarried out His laws,\nوَاَقَمْتَ الصَّلَاةَ\nWA AQAMTAS SALAAH\noffered the prayers,\nوَاٰتَيْتَ الزَّكَاةَ\nWA AATAYTAZ ZAKAAH\npaid the zakat,\nوَاَمَرْتَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ\nWA AMARTA BIL MA'ROOF\nenjoined the right,\nوَنَهَيْتَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ\nWA NAHAYTA A'NIL MUNKAR\nforbade the wrong,\nوَجَاهَدْتَ فِيْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ صَابِرًا نَاصِحًا\nWA JAAHADTA FEE SABEELILLAAHI SAABIRAN NAASIHAA\nand strove in Allah’s way with steadfastness and well-wishing,\nمُجْتَهِدًا مُحْتَسِبًا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ عَظِيْمَ الْاَجْرِ حَتّٰى اَتَاكَ الْيَقِيْنُ\nMUJTAHIDAN MUHTASIBAN I'NDALLAAHI A'ZEEMAL AJRI HATTAA ATAAKAL YAQEEN\nand with painstakingness and with the intention of seeking the great reward of Allah until death came upon you.\nفَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ دَفَعَكَ عَنْ حَقِّكَ\nFALA'ANALLAAHU MAN DAFA'AKA A'N HAQQIK\nSo, Allah’s curse be upon those who deprived you of your right\nوَاَزَالَكَ عَنْ مَقَامِكَ\nWA AZAALAKA A'N MAQAAMIK\nand upon those who took you away from your position.\nوَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ بَلَغَهٗ ذٰلِكَ فَرَضِيَ بِهٖ\nWA LA'ANALLAAHU MAN BALAGHAHOO DHAALIKA FARADIYA BIH\nAllah’s curse be upon every one who, when informed about this, accepted it.\nاُشْهِدُ اللّٰهَ وَمَلَاۤئِكَتَهٗ وَاَنْبِيَاۤءَهٗ وَرُسُلَهٗ\nUSH-HIDULLAAHA WA MALAA'IKATAHOO WA ANBIYAA'AHOO WA RUSULAH\nI call Allah, His angels, His Prophets, and His Messengers to witness for me that\nاَنِّيْ وَلِيٌّ لِمَنْ وَالَاكَ\nANNEE WALIYYUN LIMAN WAALAAK\nI am the friend of him who is loyal to you\nوَعَدُوٌّ لِمَنْ عَادَاكَ\nWA A'DUWWUN LIMAN A'ADAAK\nand the enemy of him who antagonizes you.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace and Allah’s mercy and blessings be upon you.\nLean over the tomb, kiss it and say:\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ تَسْمَعُ كَلَامِيْ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA TASMA'U KALAAMEE\nI bear witness that you can hear my words\nوَتَشْهَدُ مَقَامِيْ\nWA TASH-HADU MAQAAMEE\nand see my place.\nوَاَشْهَدُ لَكَ يَا وَلِيَّ اللّٰهِ بِالْبَلَاغِ وَالْاَدَاۤءِ\nWA ASH-HADU LAKA YAA WALIYYALLAAHI BIL BALAAGHI WAL ADAA'\nAnd I testify to you, O Allah’s friend, that you conveyed and fulfilled.\nيَا مَوْلَايَ يَا حُجَّةَ اللّٰهِ\nYAA MAWLAAYA YAA HUJJATALLAAH\nO my master! O Allah’s argument!\nيَا اَمِيْنَ اللّٰهِ يَا وَلِيَّ اللّٰهِ\nYAA AMEENALLAAHI YAA WALIYYALLAAH\nO Allah’s trustee! O Allah’s friend!\nاِنَّ بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَ اللّٰهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ ذُنُوْبًا\nINNA BAYNEE WA BAYNALLAAHI A'ZZA WA JALLA DHUNOOBAA\nBetween me and Allah, to Whom all might and majesty belong, there are sins\nقَدْ اَثْقَلَتْ ظَهْرِيْ\nQAD ATHQALAT ZAHREE\nthat have overburdened my back\nوَمَنَعَتْنِيْ مِنَ الرُّقَادِ\nWA MANA'ATNEE MINAR RUQAAD\nand deprived me of sleep;\nوَذِكْرُهَا يُقَلْقِلُ اَحْشَاۤئِيْ\nWA DHIKRUHAA YUQALQILU AHSHAA'EE\nwhenever I remember them, even my insides shiver.\nوَقَدْ هَرَبْتُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ وَاِلَيْكَ\nWA QAD HARABTU ILALLAAHI A'ZZA WA JALLA WA ILAYK\nI thus flee to Allah, to Whom all might and majesty belong, and to you.\nفَبِحَقِّ مَنِ ائْتَمَنَكَ عَلٰى سِرِّهٖ\nFABIHAQQI MANIT AMANAKA A'LAA SIRRIH\nI beg you in the name of Him Who has entrusted you with His secrets,\nوَاسْتَرْعَاكَ اَمْرَ خَلْقِهٖ\nWASTAR'AAKA AMRA KHALQIH\nappointed you as the supervisor over the affairs of His creatures,\nوَقَرَنَ طَاعَتَكَ بِطَاعَتِهٖ\nWA QARANA TAA'ATAKA BITAA'ATIH\nmatched the obedience to you to the obedience to Him,\nوَمُوَالَاتَكَ بِمُوَالَاتِهٖ\nWA MUWAALAATAKA BIMUWAALAATIH\nand matched the loyalty to you to the loyalty to Him\nكُنْ لِيْ اِلَى اللّٰهِ شَفِيْعًا\nKUN LEE ILALLAAHI SHAFEE'AA\nthat you may intercede for me before Allah,\nوَمِنَ النَّارِ مُجِيْرًا\nWA MINAN NAARI MUJEERAA\nrescue me from Hellfire,\nوَعَلَى الدَّهْرِ ظَهِيْرًا\nWA A'LAD DAHRI ZAHEERAA\nand aid me against the vicissitudes of my time.\nLean over the tomb again, kiss it and say:\nيَا وَلِيَّ اللّٰهِ\nYAA WALIYYALLAAH\nO Allah’s friend!\nيَا حُجَّةَ اللّٰهِ\nYAA HUJJATALLAAH\nO Allah’s argument!\nيَا بَابَ حِطَّةِ اللّٰهِ\nYAA BAABA HITTATILLAAH\nO Allah’s door of forgiveness!\nوَلِيُّكَ وَزَاۤئِرُكَ\nWALIYYUKA WA ZAA'IRUK\nYour adherent and your visitor,\nوَاللَّاۤئِذُ بِقَبْرِكَ\nWAL LAA'IDHU BIQABRIK\nwho seeks refuge at your tomb,\nوَالنَّازِلُ بِفِنَاۤئِكَ\nWAN NAAZILU BIFINAA'IK\nwho has alighted in your courtyard,\nوَالْمُنِيْخُ رَحْلَهٗ فِيْ جِوَارِكَ\nWAL MUNEEKHU RAHLAHOO FEE JIWAARIK\nand who has set down his saddle in your vicinity,\nيَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تَشْفَعَ لَهٗ اِلَى اللّٰهِ فِي قَضَاۤءِ حَاجَتِهٖ\nYAS'ALUKA AN TASHFA'A LAHOO ILALLAAHI FEE QADAA'I HAAJATIH\nasks you to intercede for him with Allah in granting his need\nوَنُجْحِ طَلِبَتِهٖ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nWA NUJHI TALIBATIHEE FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\nand fulfilling his requests in this world and the hereafter,\nفَاِنَّ لَكَ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ الْجَاهَ الْعَظِيْمَ\nFA-INNA LAKA I'NDALLAAHIL JAAHAL A'ZEEM\nbecause you enjoy an enormous position with Allah,\nوَالشَّفَاعَةَ الْمَقْبُوْلَةَ\nWASH SHAFAA'ATAL MAQBOOLAH\nas well as admitted right of intercession.\nفَاجْعَلْنِيْ يَا مَوْلَايَ مِنْ هَمِّكَ\nFAJ'ALNEE YAA MAWLAAYA MIN HAMMIK\nSo, O my master, include me with those for whom you care\nوَاَدْخِلْنِيْ فِي حِزْبِكَ\nWA ADKHILNEE FEE HIZBIK\nand include me with your party.\nوَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰى ضَجِيْعَيْكَ اٰدَمَ وَنُوْحٍ\nWAS SALAAMU A'LAYKA WA A'LAA DAJEE'AYKA AADAMA WA NOOH\nPeace be upon you and upon your partners in place; Adam and Noah.\nوَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰى وَلَدَيْكَ الْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ\nWAS SALAAMU A'LAYKA WA A'LAA WALADAYKAL HASANI WAL HUSAYN\nPeace be upon you and upon your two sons; al-Hasan and al-Husayn,\nوَعَلَى الْاَئِمَّةِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِكَ\nWA A'LAL A'IMMATIT TAAHIREENA MIN DHURRIYYATIK\nand upon the immaculate Imams from your progeny.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAllah’s mercy and blessings be upon you.\nThen pray six units of ziyarat prayer, two at a time: two for Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.), two for Prophet Adam (a.s.) and two for Prophet Noah (a.s.).\nThen supplicate Allah as earnestly as you can.",
  "merits": "Al-Shahid, Shaykh al-Mufid and Sayyid Ibn Tawus report that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) visited the tomb of Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.) with this ziyarat on 17 Rabi al-Awwal, the birthday of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), and taught it to the trustworthy scholar Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Thaqafi.\n\nThe author of al-Mazar al-Kabir says this ziyarat is for the seventeenth at sunrise. Allamah al-Majlisi calls it one of the best forms of ziyarat, reported through reliable chains and recorded in authentic books. Some of the narrations that report it do not tie it to this day, so it may be recited at the tomb of Imam Ali (a.s.) at any time.\n\nAfter the prayer, supplicate earnestly: prayers are answered at this place, Allah willing.\n\nWhy Imam Ali (a.s.) is visited on the Prophet's days: on occasions of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), such as his birthday and the day of his Mission (al-Mab'ath), it is the tomb of Imam Ali (a.s.) that is especially recommended for ziyarat, because of the close bond and the unity between the two. To visit Imam Ali (a.s.) is to visit the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.). In the verse of Mubahala Allah refers to them both as \"our selves\": \"Then say: Come, let us call our sons and your sons, our women and your women, and our selves and your selves, then let us be earnest in prayer and invoke the curse of Allah on the liars\" (3:61).\n\nShaykh Muhammad ibn al-Mashhadi reports from Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) that a Bedouin told the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that his home was far away, so when he could not come to see him he visited Ali ibn Abi Talib (a.s.), whose words comforted him. The Prophet (s.a.w.a.) answered, \"He who visits Ali has visited me; he who loves Ali has loved me; he who antagonizes Ali has antagonized me. Convey this to your people. He who intends to visit Ali has visited me, and I will reward him on the Day of Resurrection, and so will Gabriel and the righteous believers.\"\n\nImam al-Sadiq (a.s.) also said, \"Whenever you visit al-Najaf, visit there the bones of Adam (a.s.), the body of Noah (a.s.) and the body of Ali ibn Abi Talib (a.s.). You will be visiting the forefathers, Muhammad the Seal of the Prophets, and Ali the best of the successors.\""
